  "title": "CHAPTER 5: CULTURE, ART AND HERITAGE OF MAHARASHTRA",
  "order": 5,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "z9ufbqo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.1 Languages and Literature"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Marathi language and literature trace a historical continuum from ancient inscriptions and saint literature to modern literary masterpieces.",
        "The Warkari movement transformed the socio-cultural landscape of Maharashtra through devotional literature and egalitarian Bhakti philosophy.",
        "Maharashtra features prominent UNESCO World Heritage Sites including the rock-cut caves at Ajanta, Ellora, and Elephanta.",
        "The strategic military architecture of Maharashtra is defined by sea forts, hill forts, and land forts built and fortified during the Maratha Empire.",
        "Major festivals such as Ganeshotsav, Gudhi Padwa, and Ashadhi Ekadashi reflect the vibrant cultural identity of the region."
      ],
      "id": "8vxxv4u"
    },
